abstract: >-
  A machine-readable table of 40 colour electronic-paper panels across E Ink Spectra 6,
  four-colour E5 and Kaleido 3, covering 1.18 to 55 inch. For each panel the table records
  the application, panel family, colour bit depth, diagonal, active area, colour set,
  resolution, the packed size of one full frame, and the resulting pixel density.
  Image size is computed from the storage format rather than the colour count: E6 carries
  three bits of colour information in a four-bit nibble, so a frame is width x height / 2
  bytes, and all 40 rows reconcile under that rule to within one percent. No measurements
  were taken; this is a specification table, not a lab report.
